contentText:
Early during his concert Saturday night (Aug. 15) in Detroit, Bryan Adams spoke about having &#8220;the pleasure&#8221; of having Pat Benatar & Neil Giraldo supporting him on tour since last October, but noted that he&#8217;d &#8220;never had them on stage — before tonight.&#8221;

And because, as Adams told the Little Caesars Arena crowd, &#8220;this is Motown city,&#8221; he invited the Rock & Roll Hall of Fame duo to join his band onstage for the first time, delivering a spirited rendition of Stevie Wonder &#8216;s &#8220;Superstition.&#8221; Adams and Benatar shared lead vocals, while Giraldo and Adams&#8217; Keith Scott traded guitar licks. Afterwards, Adams said, “Thanks everybody. That was awesome.”

